\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Omnipresent God, whose aid
\par No one ever asked in vain,
\par Be this night about my bed,
\par Every evil thought restrain;
\par Lay Thy hand upon my soul,
\par God of my unguarded hours;
\par All my enemies control,
\par Hell, and earth, and nature's powers
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Loose me from the chains of sense,
\par Set me from the body free,
\par Draw with stronger influence
\par My unfettered soul to Thee;
\par In me, Lord, Thyself reveal,
\par Fill me with a sweet surprise:
\par Let me Thee when waking feel,
\par Let me in Thy image rise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let me of Thy life partake,
\par Thy own holiness impart,
\par O that I might sweetly wake
\par With my Saviour in my heart!
\par O that I mighgt know Thee mine!
\par O that I might Thee receive!
\par Only live the life divine,
\par Only to Thy glory live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Or if Thou my soul require
\par Ere I see the morning light,
\par Grant me, Lord, my heart's desire,
\par Perfect me in love to-night:
\par Finish Thy great work of love,
\par Cut it short in righteousness,
\par Fit me for the realms above,
\par Change, and bid me die in peace.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

